#: ../../source/semver_README.md:72
msgid "Versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:74
msgid ""
"A \"version\" is described by the `v2.0.0` specification found at "
"<https://semver.org/>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:77
msgid "A leading `\"=\"` or `\"v\"` character is stripped off and ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:79 ../../source/semver_README.md:365
msgid "Ranges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:81
msgid ""
"A `version range` is a set of `comparators` which specify versions that "
"satisfy the range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:84
msgid ""
"A `comparator` is composed of an `operator` and a `version`.  The set of "
"primitive `operators` is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:87
msgid "`<` Less than"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:88
msgid "`<=` Less than or equal to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:89
msgid "`>` Greater than"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:90
msgid "`>=` Greater than or equal to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:91
msgid ""
"`=` Equal.  If no operator is specified, then equality is assumed, so "
"this operator is optional, but MAY be included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:94
msgid ""
"For example, the comparator `>=1.2.7` would match the versions `1.2.7`, "
"`1.2.8`, `2.5.3`, and `1.3.9`, but not the versions `1.2.6` or `1.1.0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:98
msgid ""
"Comparators can be joined by whitespace to form a `comparator set`, which"
" is satisfied by the **intersection** of all of the comparators it "
"includes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:102
msgid ""
"A range is composed of one or more comparator sets, joined by `||`.  A "
"version matches a range if and only if every comparator in at least one "
"of the `||`-separated comparator sets is satisfied by the version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:106
msgid ""
"For example, the range `>=1.2.7 <1.3.0` would match the versions `1.2.7`,"
" `1.2.8`, and `1.2.99`, but not the versions `1.2.6`, `1.3.0`, or "
"`1.1.0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:110
msgid ""
"The range `1.2.7 || >=1.2.9 <2.0.0` would match the versions `1.2.7`, "
"`1.2.9`, and `1.4.6`, but not the versions `1.2.8` or `2.0.0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:113
msgid "Prerelease Tags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:115
msgid ""
"If a version has a prerelease tag (for example, `1.2.3-alpha.3`) then it "
"will only be allowed to satisfy comparator sets if at least one "
"comparator with the same `[major, minor, patch]` tuple also has a "
"prerelease tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:120
msgid ""
"For example, the range `>1.2.3-alpha.3` would be allowed to match the "
"version `1.2.3-alpha.7`, but it would *not* be satisfied by "
"`3.4.5-alpha.9`, even though `3.4.5-alpha.9` is technically \"greater "
"than\" `1.2.3-alpha.3` according to the SemVer sort rules.  The version "
"range only accepts prerelease tags on the `1.2.3` version.  The version "
"`3.4.5` *would* satisfy the range, because it does not have a prerelease "
"flag, and `3.4.5` is greater than `1.2.3-alpha.7`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:128
msgid ""
"The purpose for this behavior is twofold.  First, prerelease versions "
"frequently are updated very quickly, and contain many breaking changes "
"that are (by the author's design) not yet fit for public consumption. "
"Therefore, by default, they are excluded from range matching semantics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:134
msgid ""
"Second, a user who has opted into using a prerelease version has clearly "
"indicated the intent to use *that specific* set of alpha/beta/rc "
"versions.  By including a prerelease tag in the range, the user is "
"indicating that they are aware of the risk.  However, it is still not "
"appropriate to assume that they have opted into taking a similar risk on "
"the *next* set of prerelease versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:141
msgid ""
"Note that this behavior can be suppressed (treating all prerelease "
"versions as if they were normal versions, for the purpose of range "
"matching) by setting the `includePrerelease` flag on the options object "
"to any [functions](https://github.com/npm/node-semver#functions) that do "
"range matching."
msgstr ""

