#: ../../source/semver_README.md:299
msgid "Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:301
msgid ""
"All methods and classes take a final `options` object argument.  All "
"options in this object are `false` by default.  The options supported "
"are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:305
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`loose`  Be more forgiving about not-quite-valid semver strings. (Any "
"resulting output will always be 100% strict compliant, of course.)  For "
"backwards compatibility reasons, if the `options` argument is a boolean "
"value instead of an object, it is interpreted to be the `loose` param."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:310
msgid ""
"`includePrerelease`  Set to suppress the [default "
"behavior](https://github.com/npm/node-semver#prerelease-tags) of "
"excluding prerelease tagged versions from ranges unless they are "
"explicitly opted into."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:315
msgid ""
"Strict-mode Comparators and Ranges will be strict about the SemVer "
"strings that they parse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:318
msgid "`valid(v)`: Return the parsed version, or null if it's not valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:319
msgid ""
"`inc(v, release)`: Return the version incremented by the release type "
"(`major`,   `premajor`, `minor`, `preminor`, `patch`, `prepatch`, or "
"`prerelease`), or null if it's not valid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:322
msgid ""
"`premajor` in one call will bump the version up to the next major version"
" and down to a prerelease of that major version. `preminor`, and "
"`prepatch` work the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:325
msgid ""
"If called from a non-prerelease version, the `prerelease` will work the "
"same as `prepatch`. It increments the patch version, then makes a "
"prerelease. If the input version is already a prerelease it simply "
"increments it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:329
msgid ""
"`prerelease(v)`: Returns an array of prerelease components, or null if "
"none exist. Example: `prerelease('1.2.3-alpha.1') -> ['alpha', 1]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:331
msgid "`major(v)`: Return the major version number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:332
msgid "`minor(v)`: Return the minor version number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:333
msgid "`patch(v)`: Return the patch version number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:334
msgid ""
"`intersects(r1, r2, loose)`: Return true if the two supplied ranges or "
"comparators intersect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:336
msgid ""
"`parse(v)`: Attempt to parse a string as a semantic version, returning "
"either a `SemVer` object or `null`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:339
msgid "Comparison"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:341
msgid "`gt(v1, v2)`: `v1 > v2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:342
msgid "`gte(v1, v2)`: `v1 >= v2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:343
msgid "`lt(v1, v2)`: `v1 < v2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:344
msgid "`lte(v1, v2)`: `v1 <= v2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:345
msgid ""
"`eq(v1, v2)`: `v1 == v2` This is true if they're logically equivalent, "
"even if they're not the exact same string.  You already know how to "
"compare strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:348
msgid "`neq(v1, v2)`: `v1 != v2` The opposite of `eq`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:349
msgid ""
"`cmp(v1, comparator, v2)`: Pass in a comparison string, and it'll call "
"the corresponding function above.  `\"===\"` and `\"!==\"` do simple "
"string comparison, but are included for completeness.  Throws if an "
"invalid comparison string is provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:353
msgid ""
"`compare(v1, v2)`: Return `0` if `v1 == v2`, or `1` if `v1` is greater, "
"or `-1` if `v2` is greater.  Sorts in ascending order if passed to "
"`Array.sort()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:355
msgid ""
"`rcompare(v1, v2)`: The reverse of compare.  Sorts an array of versions "
"in descending order when passed to `Array.sort()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:357
msgid ""
"`diff(v1, v2)`: Returns difference between two versions by the release "
"type (`major`, `premajor`, `minor`, `preminor`, `patch`, `prepatch`, or "
"`prerelease`), or null if the versions are the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:361
msgid "Comparators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:363
msgid "`intersects(comparator)`: Return true if the comparators intersect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:367
msgid "`validRange(range)`: Return the valid range or null if it's not valid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:368
msgid ""
"`satisfies(version, range)`: Return true if the version satisfies the "
"range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:370
msgid ""
"`maxSatisfying(versions, range)`: Return the highest version in the list "
"that satisfies the range, or `null` if none of them do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:372
msgid ""
"`minSatisfying(versions, range)`: Return the lowest version in the list "
"that satisfies the range, or `null` if none of them do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:374
msgid ""
"`minVersion(range)`: Return the lowest version that can possibly match "
"the given range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:376
msgid ""
"`gtr(version, range)`: Return `true` if version is greater than all the "
"versions possible in the range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:378
msgid ""
"`ltr(version, range)`: Return `true` if version is less than all the "
"versions possible in the range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:380
msgid ""
"`outside(version, range, hilo)`: Return true if the version is outside "
"the bounds of the range in either the high or low direction.  The `hilo` "
"argument must be either the string `'>'` or `'<'`.  (This is the function"
" called by `gtr` and `ltr`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:384
msgid ""
"`intersects(range)`: Return true if any of the ranges comparators "
"intersect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:386
msgid ""
"Note that, since ranges may be non-contiguous, a version might not be "
"greater than a range, less than a range, *or* satisfy a range!  For "
"example, the range `1.2 <1.2.9 || >2.0.0` would have a hole from `1.2.9` "
"until `2.0.0`, so the version `1.2.10` would not be greater than the "
"range (because `2.0.1` satisfies, which is higher), nor less than the "
"range (since `1.2.8` satisfies, which is lower), and it also does not "
"satisfy the range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:394
msgid ""
"If you want to know if a version satisfies or does not satisfy a range, "
"use the `satisfies(version, range)` function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:397
msgid "Coercion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:399
msgid "`coerce(version)`: Coerces a string to semver if possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/semver_README.md:401
msgid ""
"This aims to provide a very forgiving translation of a non-semver string "
"to semver. It looks for the first digit in a string, and consumes all "
"remaining characters which satisfy at least a partial semver (e.g., `1`, "
"`1.2`, `1.2.3`) up to the max permitted length (256 characters).  Longer "
"versions are simply truncated (`4.6.3.9.2-alpha2` becomes `4.6.3`).  All "
"surrounding text is simply ignored (`v3.4 replaces v3.3.1` becomes "
"`3.4.0`).  Only text which lacks digits will fail coercion (`version one`"
" is not valid).  The maximum  length for any semver component considered "
"for coercion is 16 characters; longer components will be ignored "
"(`10000000000000000.4.7.4` becomes `4.7.4`).  The maximum value for any "
"semver component is `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER || (2**53 - 1)`; higher "
"value components are invalid (`9999999999999999.4.7.4` is likely "
"invalid)."
msgstr ""

